# This repo is cloned on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. For everything in this directory that is CATASTROPHIC
# rather than cosmetic:
#
#   *.sh              a CRLF shebang makes `#!/usr/bin/env sh` into
#                     `sh\r`, and the kernel reports "bad interpreter: No such
#                     file or directory" — for a file that plainly exists.
#   *.py              embedded in the shell scripts via heredoc; a stray \r
#                     inside a string is invisible and corrupts values silently
#                     (see the GRID_PX story in build/02-dem.sh).
#   Caddyfile/service  parsed on Linux by Caddy and systemd.
#
# Forcing LF here keeps the working tree byte-identical to what runs in the
# containers and on the VPS.
#   config.env*     SOURCED by every build script (`. config.env`). With CRLF,
#                   BASEMAP_HOST becomes "tiles.sgss.ca<CR>" and every URL
#                   built from it is quietly wrong. The example is the file
#                   operators copy to make the real one, so it must ship LF.
*.sh            text eol=lf
config.env*     text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
Caddyfile*      text eol=lf
*.Containerfile text eol=lf
